# Needs a reports server. Start the AppHost (aspire start), which passes the server's address to the
# app; the dashboard and `aspire describe` show the app's URL. Or run the app on its own against any
# server: dotnet run -- --ConnectionStrings:reports-server=http://localhost:8080
@RemoteReportServer_HostAddress = http://localhost:5294

### A Blazor report from ExampleTemplates, rendered here and converted on the reports server
POST {{RemoteReportServer_HostAddress}}/reports/reportwithrepeatingheaderperpage

### Any HTML document, converted on the reports server
POST {{RemoteReportServer_HostAddress}}/html-to-pdf
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "html": "<!DOCTYPE html><h1>Hello, PDF</h1><p>Converted by the reports server.</p>"
}
